If you have been in the IT industry for any length of time, you've heard the argument "software is not your core competency".  This
is the argument that vendors make when they are convincing IT shops to outsource their software development teams.  Leave the IT problems to us
so you can focus on your core business, but it financial services, education, or whatever.  
And it worked.  Shops all across Canada drank the blue cool-aid, and software developers vanished from the building.
Next came the COTS (common off the shelf) argument.  Why write software at all, they said. Just buy this COTS solution and all you need to do 
is install, configure and run.  